  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A Nightshelf ice-reader who inherited study of the Thaw-Paths Medallion, a glass artifact of disputed origin, from ☽'Ilsancuia Depth-walker after the elder scholar's death. Where ☽'Ilsancuia had tended the medallion gently over a decade — she maintained it was suffering — ☽'Ilun spent three seasons forcing it to yield its concealed pathways, employing ice-reading techniques the Aurora Stack no longer taught. The medallion was not cooperative. He persisted.
    
    It showed him two maps. The surface layer traced the Midnight Claws' fire-core smuggling network through the Aurora Stack. The deeper layer, visible only under altered light, mapped approach vectors through the Stack's eastern ridge and marked defensive positions that had been deliberately dismantled from the inside prior to the Shattered-Spire Assault — evidence implicating figures the confession that followed was carefully structured to protect.
    
    ☽'Ilun reported his findings to someone within the Stack. Two nights later, agents of the Midnight Claws killed him. The body was fed to a thermal vent. The throat wound was shaped to match a claw-mark, which is either a signature or a misdirection; the record does not distinguish.
    
    Shadow-Broker Nyla, leader of the Midnight Claws, later confessed to his murder during a formal proceeding at the Lens-Cathedral. She devoted a single phrase to him within a three-hour accounting of thirty winters of operations: "a complication resolved." The confession itself, as Auditor Yunjoushong of the Aurora Stack subsequently discovered, was orchestrated to contain the medallion's deeper revelations — lesser crimes offered to shield greater ones.
    
    He became a line-item. The medallion outlasted him.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771592932508_0", anchor: "defensive positions that had been deliberately dismantled from the inside prior to the Shattered-Spire Assault", text: "The medallion mapped what the Foundation Depths have long implied but never stated cleanly: the Shattered-Spire Assault succeeded in part because someone inside Aurora Stack cleared its path. The coordinated Nightshelf intelligence operations active during the Orca Incursion — operations the heroic narratives never acknowledge — had assets positioned throughout the Stack's eastern defenses. Whether those assets dismantled positions to aid the orca or to ensure certain outcomes during the counterattack is precisely the question Nyla's confession was built to foreclose. ☽'Ilun died holding the answer to a question most scholars do not know to ask.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771592932508_1", anchor: "reported his findings to someone within the Stack", text: "Two nights. Information crosses from an ice-reader's study to a Midnight Claws kill-order in two nights. Either the Claws maintained surveillance on ☽'Ilun already — possible, given the medallion's contents — or the 'someone within the Stack' was the conduit. I could not determine which. The vagueness is mine, not a stylistic choice.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592932508_2", anchor: "a complication resolved", text: "Three seasons of work. A scholar's life. Three words in a three-hour confession, calibrated to the syllable. Nyla was many things, but she understood the weight of proportion — that burying a name in a list is more thorough than omitting it. Omissions invite questions. Line-items do not.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
